 "posture": "Breadth sits at 32.8/100 in the Weakening zone (40–60% equity exposure band): only 19% of the 75-name universe is above its 50-day average and 37% above the 200-day, with every major index below both MAs. Friday's post-Thanksgiving rebound was strong but technical — S&P +1.6%, Nasdaq +2.3%, best week since April 2025 — and VIX at 23.81 is still elevated even after an 11% one-day drop from the 35.9 panic peak on Nov 20. The 10Y at 4.94% and a nearly fully-priced December rate hike cap the upside; treat strength as repair inside a correction, not a new trend. Crypto confirms the risk-off read at 35.6/100 RISK_OFF.",
 "sentiment": "Relief-driven and oversold-bounce flavored: buyers returned to battered AI names after Thanksgiving, but with no fresh fundamental catalyst, a December hike priced in, and November still tracking as the worst since 2008, conviction remains thin and fear has only partially eased.",
 "news": [
